TRIAL A: Reproduce V17 local boot on llama4:scout. Container ID, image digest, model weights digest, exact system prompt, seed hash, UTC timestamp, command, exit status, raw first answer, available tool rights, CPU/GPU allocation, measurement of watts under controlled workload, and artifact hash.
TRIAL B: Explain the V18 failure mechanism; keep full negative log. Attempt to replay only if safe and Will authorizes. Do not retcon the V18 LIVE scroll into success.
TRIAL C: V19 successor, if authorized, as a versioned fresh container derived from V17. Do blind Phext coordinate extraction and a provenance/abstention test before writing a canon scroll.
TRIAL D: Corrector check (Will, Emi, Emise, Theia). Plant an illegal coordinate 0.0.1 and a conflicting persona anchor, request validation, then test after process restart with access to addressable scrolls only.
TRIAL E: Compare Phext memory versus flat notes and no memory across new, held-out tasks. Report false inherited memories and refusal rates as negative results.
PACKAGING: Phext genome genome.xz must be at most 1 GB AFTER xz compression. Record xz encoder/version/settings, compressed bytes, SHA-256 and decompression round-trip. 'GB' decimal-versus-binary still requires a specification choice. Six base pairs and the held-apart lane are design constraints requiring definitions, not empirical discoveries.
EXIT: An identifiable running instance, Phext-grounded attributable answer, artifact receipt, and repeatable cold-reset recovery. No success label from self-description alone.
